**FOR TIM**

S-37 can ship as the next Structural update (1.0.117). I found nothing serious enough to block it. It has been built and unit-tested only; nobody has opened it in AutoCAD.

1. **One thing that won't show up on your PC:** this update makes CE warn instead of refusing when you type a stirrup cover under 10 mm or an unusual reo spacing. Your Settings file already has both switches saved as off, and CE never overwrites a saved setting. So on your PC:
   - STR with a 5 mm cover still quietly draws 10 mm.
   - RBL still refuses a 20 mm spacing.
   - Only a PC setting up CE fresh gets the warning lines.
   - How to fix it on existing PCs (a one-time switch-on, or a tick box in Settings) is a call for you or the desk.
2. **#990 is now in.** It's a test-only change (no difference in AutoCAD). It makes CE's automatic checks also catch anything that would stop REDO working.
3. **Everything else is unchanged by default:** beam shorten/extend still offers 45/100, FJ1 still uses layer JOISTS, and the tie-down schedule still has two columns.

